From 63a3cba1b0c1451d2245b7ce898dd38b04b00efd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:51:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0324 -- say NOT COLLECTED instead of
 printing zeros

The [p12-audio] instrument has two gates and they are not the same one.
The PRINT gate is FLIP_INSTR; the COLLECT gate is P12_AUDIO_INSTR,
checked inside the RAII timers' destructors. Open only the print gate
and every field emits zero, counts included.

That is the most dangerous output in this codebase. Every other failure
here announces itself by ABSENCE -- a missing line, a refused cell, a
silent skip. This one emits a perfectly formed statistic, with the right
field names, the right block count and a number in every slot, whose
actual meaning is "nothing was sampled". An absence invites a second
look. A zero closes the question.

It cost a real reading on 2026-08-21. [p12-audio] was quoted as evidence
that audio was free; audio later measured at 2.35 ms of a 35.5 ms frame,
the largest unbucketed cost anyone had found. What gave it away was the
COUNTS being zero rather than merely the microseconds, and only because
someone checked rather than reading the times and moving on.

So the emit now checks its own collect gate and says what it means. The
message names the other hint, and states explicitly that zeros would have
meant "not sampled" rather than "measured as zero" -- because the next
person to see this line will be reading it in a log, without the source
in front of them.

Also braces the else. The prior form was a braceless else before a
multi-line macro: correct today, and silently wrong the moment anyone
adds a second statement.

No behaviour change when P12_AUDIO_INSTR is set. The zeros case was
never a measurement, so nothing that was previously true stops being so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index e68a2273..2cee0637 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -2601,13 +2601,43 @@ void _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit()
   // SDL/0054 [p12-sdl ...] emit line (sdl-engine's lane).
   if (_abl_flip_instr())
   {
-    LOG_INFO("[p12-audio n=100 midi_tick_us={} midi_tick_count={} pixtone_play_us={} pixtone_play_count={} pixtone_stop_us={} pixtone_stop_count={}]",
+    // DOS-PORT (patch 0324): this instrument has TWO gates and they are not
+    // the same one. The PRINT gate is FLIP_INSTR (immediately above); the
+    // COLLECT gate is P12_AUDIO_INSTR, checked inside the RAII timers'
+    // destructors in diagnostic_timers.h. Open only the print gate and every
+    // field below emits zero -- counts included.
+    //
+    // That is the most dangerous output this codebase produces. Every other
+    // failure here announces itself by ABSENCE: a missing line, a refused
+    // cell, a silent skip. This one emits a perfectly formed statistic --
+    // right field names, right block count, a number in every slot -- whose
+    // meaning is "nothing was sampled". An absence invites a second look; a
+    // zero closes the question.
+    //
+    // It cost a real reading on 2026-08-21: [p12-audio] was quoted as
+    // evidence that audio was free, and audio later measured at 2.35 ms of a
+    // 35.5 ms frame. The counts being zero rather than merely the
+    // microseconds is what gave it away, and only because someone checked.
+    //
+    // So say so instead of printing zeros.
+    if (!_abl_p12_audio_instr())
+    {
+      LOG_INFO("[p12-audio n=100 NOT COLLECTED -- set "
+               "SDL_HINT_DOS_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 to accumulate. "
+               "FLIP_INSTR opens the print gate only; the timers sample "
+               "under their own gate. Zeros here would mean 'not sampled', "
+               "NOT 'measured as zero'.]");
+    }
+    else
+    {
+      LOG_INFO("[p12-audio n=100 midi_tick_us={} midi_tick_count={} pixtone_play_us={} pixtone_play_count={} pixtone_stop_us={} pixtone_stop_count={}]",
              (unsigned long)(NXE::Diag::g_p12_midi_tick_accum_ns_block / 1000ULL),
              NXE::Diag::g_p12_midi_tick_count_block,
              (unsigned long)(NXE::Diag::g_p12_pixtone_play_accum_ns_block / 1000ULL),
              NXE::Diag::g_p12_pixtone_play_count_block,
              (unsigned long)(NXE::Diag::g_p12_pixtone_stop_accum_ns_block / 1000ULL),
-             NXE::Diag::g_p12_pixtone_stop_count_block);
+               NXE::Diag::g_p12_pixtone_stop_count_block);
+    }
   }
   // patch 0131: reset all 6 P12 counters unconditionally -- sample
   // contents accumulated since prior reset; idx-style reset zeroes
